  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 125 AM MST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nWednesday - Saturday: For midweek into the start of the weekend, \nsome active weather makes a return for south central and \nsoutheastern Colorado. The pattern will become more unsettled, as \nadditional waves pass over the region, one generally Wednesday-early \nThursday, and another Friday-early Saturday. These features will \nbring heightened precipitation chances to the area, particularly the \nWednesday-Thursday system given a stronger and more structured wave. \nThere is potential the second wave Friday-Saturday brings very \nlittle, if any, additional precipitation given unfavorable storm \nstructure and timing of its passage behind the midweek system. \nBetween these features, dry and quieter weather can be anticipated. \nOtherwise, expect breezy winds, especially during the wave passages, \nand periods of partly to mostly cloudy skies. Temperatures are \nanticipated to remain fairly stable, with much of the region \nhovering near seasonal values.\n\nSunday - Monday: For the end of the weekend and into early next \nweek, quiet weather again makes a return to south central and \nsoutheastern Colorado. Ridging looks to build across the area during \nthis period, which will bring greater descent and drier air. This \nwill mean dry and quiet weather conditions for the region. Ensemble \nmodel guidance are in solid agreement about this pattern evolution, \nleading to high (70%) confidence in this pattern progression. Beyond \nall of that, mostly clear skies and lighter winds can be expected. \nLooking at temperatures, a warming trend begins, with much of south \ncentral and southeastern Colorado warming to above seasonal values.",
